WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.060
- [Instructor] What we're
going to do in this video

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.440
is dig a little bit deeper

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.250
into our understanding of multiplication.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.510
And just as an example,

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.130
we're going to use four times seven.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.530
And some of you might know
what four times seven is,

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.940
but even in this case,

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.420
I think you might get
something from this video

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.070
because we're gonna think
about how you can break down

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.050
a multiplication question
into simpler parts,

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.470
and that's going to be useful
well beyond four times seven.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.440
It's going to be useful in your future

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.630
when you're tackling more
and more complicated things.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.720
Now there's a couple of
ways that we can visualize

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.410
four times seven.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.110
My favorite way is to
visualize it with angry cats,

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:44.178
so let's bring on the angry cats.

00:00:44.178 --> 00:00:45.710
(imitates cats meowing)

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.140
Yep, they're still angry.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.460
And we can see that
this is a representation

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.320
of four times seven.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.490
We have four rows right over here.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.340
Four rows,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.060
and each of those rows have seven cats.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.440
And so you can see that right over here,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.920
each of those rows has seven cats.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.300
Some people would call
this a four by seven grid

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.320
or four by seven array,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.600
however you want to view it,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.470
but if someone were to ask
you what's the total number

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.960
of cats, it would be four
rows times seven columns,

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.530
four times seven.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.760
Now another way to
represent four times seven

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.580
is also with a tape diagram.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.530
You might see something like this,

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:29.960
where here, we're visualizing
it as seven fours,

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.830
or you could view it as
four plus four plus four

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:35.360
plus four plus four plus four plus four.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.430
Now that's all well and good
and you can add that up,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.570
if you like,

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:40.870
but what I promised you is
that we would figure out ways

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.330
to break down things

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.920
that might simplify things in the future.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.360
Well what if you didn't know
what four times seven is,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.650
but you knew what four times five is

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.180
and you knew what four times two is?

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.760
Well what's interesting is
that seven is five plus two,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.760
so what if we tried to first
figure out this many cats,

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:05.950
so four rows and five
columns right over there,

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.300
and then we tried to figure out

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.360
this many cats?

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.450
Four rows and two columns.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.660
And you can see that it's the
exact same number of cats.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.860
So one way to think about
it is four times seven

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.420
is the exact same thing as four times,

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.590
and I'm gonna use parentheses,
and that just means

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:30.110
to do that part first,
is equal to four times,

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:30.960
instead of seven,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.970
I could write that as five plus two,

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.530
'cause that's what seven is,

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.640
so all this is saying is four time seven

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:41.450
is the same thing as
four times five plus two,

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.830
where you do the five plus two first,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.290
'cause we have those
parentheses around it,

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.830
and five plus two is,
indeed, equal to seven,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.830
and we can see that that is
equivalent to the total number

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.780
of cats that we have here,

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.160
which we could view as
what we just circled off

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.850
in this orangeish pink color

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.410
which would be four rows of five,

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.320
so that would be equal to four times five.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.780
Four times five,

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:10.780
and then to that, we can add
this second group of cat heads

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.160
or angry cat heads,

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.630
and that is four rows of two.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.800
So that's four times two,

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.540
and we could put parentheses if we want,

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.590
just to make it a little
bit more readable.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.980
Now why did I do that?

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.210
Well, some folks might
find four times five

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.340
a little bit more straightforward.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.850
I could skip count by five.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.260
I can go five, 10, 15, 20.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.920
Also four times two might be a

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.110
little bit more straightforward,

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.560
and so it could be easier to say hey,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.770
this is just going to be four times five,

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:44.770
which is 20, plus four times
two, which is equal to eight,

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.593
and so that is just
going to be equal to 28.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.670
And you could have thought
about it the same way down here

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.500
with what is sometimes
called a tape diagram.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.420
We could say, all right,

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.770
if I have five fours,

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.370
that's this mount right over here.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.230
That is the four times the five,

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:05.590
and then I could add
that to the two fours,

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.590
the four times the two right over here,

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.600
and that's another way to
get to four times seven.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.020
So the big picture here is
even if you're not dealing

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.980
with four times seven,
if you're not dealing

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.160
with angry cats, and in most of our lives,

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.970
we actually try to avoid angry cats,

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.190
there might be a way to
break down the numbers

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:25.740
that you're multiplying into ones

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.050
that you might be more familiar with.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.610
I'll give you one more example.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.340
Let's say someone were to ask you, well,

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:37.180
what is six times nine?

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.270
Pause this video and see
if you can break this down

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.373
in some useful way.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.420
Well, maybe you know what six times 10 is,

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.480
and you also know what six times one is,

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.650
so you could rerwrite nine

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:53.370
as 10 minus one.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.890
Well then this would
mean that six times nine

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.720
is the same thing as
six times 10 minus one.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.120
Based on exactly what we just did up here,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.030
that says that this whole thing

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:07.090
is going to be the same
thing as six times 10.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.530
Six times 10

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.560
minus six times one.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.610
One way to think about it is,

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.060
I just distributed the six.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.740
That's the distributive
property right over there,

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:22.520
and then six times 10 is equal to 60,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.750
and then six times one is equal to six.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.250
And it might be easier for me to say, hey,

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.040
16 minus six in my head,

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.670
that's equal to 54.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.050
So I know what some of you are thinking.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:34.180
Six times nine seems so clean,

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.030
and now I've involved all
of this other symbolism,

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.980
symbols, and I've written
down more numbers,

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:40.813
but at the end of the day,

00:05:40.813 --> 00:05:42.000
I'm trying to give you skills

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.440
for breaking down problems

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.730
and including ways that you might want

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:45.563
to do it in your head.

00:05:45.563 --> 00:05:46.730
If you're like, hey, I'm kind of foggy

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.310
on what six times nine is,

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.710
but six times 10, hey, I know that's 60,

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.220
and six times one, of course, that's six,

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.220
well what if I view this
as six times 10 minus one?

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.470
And then I could tackle it and get 54.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.303
And once again,

00:05:59.303 --> 00:06:00.650
you might know six times nine.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.530
You might know four times seven,

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:03.470
but in the future,

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.670
it might be useful for
bigger and bigger numbers

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.820
to think about how
could I break this down?

